<article class="env-definition" id="0APD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0APD">Definition <span data-tag="0APD">39.21.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : (U', R', s', t', c') \to (U, R, s, t, c)$ be a morphism of groupoid schemes over $S$. We say $f$ is <em>cartesian</em>, or that <em>$(U', R', s', t', c')$ is cartesian over $(U, R, s, t, c)$</em>, if the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ R' \ar[r]_ f \ar[d]_{s'} &  R \ar[d]^ s \\  U' \ar[r]^ f &  U }  \]
</div>
  <p> is a fibre square in the category of schemes. A <em>morphism of groupoid schemes cartesian over $(U, R, s, t, c)$</em> is a morphism of groupoid schemes compatible with the structure morphisms towards $(U, R, s, t, c)$. </p>
</article>